ring  capture events Pokemon counter your  pokeball throws with dodges and blocks  it's also common to approach a gym that  is currently in the midst of a power  struggle indicated by the amusing Looney  Tunes inspired whirlwind animation when  you join the fight it truly feels like a  team effort to see your buddies pokémon  battling at the far side of the arena  Pokemon goes after mentioned strengths  can't hide the fact that its initial  iteration is a buggy mess crash has come  during monster captures GPS  reconnections  and even when you're taking a screenshot  these issues occur often enough to cause  immense frustration but not enough to  make you want to give up altogether  Pokemon bows social hooks are that  strong if Pokemon goes initial public  reception is anything to go by its  ability to draw players from multiple  generations and varied gaming  backgrounds together is a game worthy of  attention when it works Pokemon go feels  like a natural evolution for the series  very much a product of the times without  making the main line series obsolete its  bugs and high battery consumption do not  outweigh the old but new thrill of  capturing Pikachu at a local park or  vanquishing a Snorlax while conquering a  gym
 

